            "source": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/13212#discussion_r4293595796",
            "head": "a661e450e81c71ee8d60f1f6a246ad8e3a37e513",
            "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
            "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Unnamed controls pass the lint**\n\nThe naming lint accepts properties that never reach `Accessible.name`. For example, `PanelSlider` and `ToggleSwitch` only use `accessibleName`, but this table also accepts `tooltipText` and `label`. A caller can therefore pass the check while leaving its control unnamed. Match each entry to the component's actual name fallback, and add negative fi",
            "review_bot": true
          },
          {
            "token": "review-comment:4306824940:2026-10-18T11:23:38Z:",
            "type": "review-comment",
            "source": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/13212#discussion_r4306824940",
            "head": "4c66862157bad42a3a71ebba1f1af2d6911c21b3",
            "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
            "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Escaped icons pass as names**\n\nThe naming lint accepts `BarIconButton { accessibleName: \"\\ue900\" }` even though its name is only an icon. `tokens()` keeps the escape as ASCII characters, so `glyph_string()` returns false and the name passes. This leaves screen reader users with an unreadable name despite a passing test.\n\nDecode QML Unicode escapes before checking glyphs, and add a",
            "review_bot": true
          },
          {
            "token": "review-comment:4308149471:2026-10-18T18:17:59Z:",
            "type": "review-comment",
            "source": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/13212#discussion_r4308149471",
            "head": "fbaecdd2aaf2f946c691ffd928ccb304aa32cdb7",
            "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
            "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Unnamed buttons pass the check**\n\nThe naming lint skips any `Button` whose explicit `text` is not a glyph, including `text: \"\"`. Thus `Button { iconText: \"\\ue900\"; text: \"\" }` passes without a name, even though `Button.accessibleName` resolves to an empty string. This leaves a gap in the check meant to catch unnamed controls for screen-reader users.\n\nOnly skip buttons with non-emp",
            "review_bot": true
          },
          {
            "token": "review-comment:4328450278:2026-10-20T18:03:47Z:",
            "type": "review-comment",
            "source": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/13212#discussion_r4328450278",
            "head": "4c66862157bad42a3a71ebba1f1af2d6911c21b3",
            "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
            "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Actions report false selection**\n\n`CursorSurface` marks every named row as selectable and uses `current` as its selected state. This includes ordinary actions such as Dropbox login and file opening. In Tailscale's copy menu, moving the keyboard cursor also reports a selection before anything is copied. Screen-reader users therefore hear highlighting described as a completed choice",
            "review_bot": true
          },
          {
            "token": "review-comment:4328450293:2026-10-20T18:03:47Z:",
            "type": "review-comment",
            "source": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/13212#discussion_r4328450293",
            "head": "4c66862157bad42a3a71ebba1f1af2d6911c21b3",
            "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
            "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Two bands report selected**\n\n`BandPill` opts into `Button` selection, which reports `selected || active`. When the user changes bands, `bandEffective` immediately becomes the requested band while `bandCurrent` still names the old band during reconnect. Screen-reader users therefore hear both pills announced as selected.\n\nOverride `Accessible.selected` here to follow only `selected",
